{
  "title": "Sessionise a User's Events",
  "topic": "sql-subqueries-windows",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "language": "sql",
  "dataset": "events",
  "description": "Split each user's events into sessions wherever there is a gap of 30 minutes or more.",
  "statement": "A **session** is a run of one user's events in which no two consecutive events are **30 minutes or more** apart (a gap of exactly 30 minutes starts a new session). Events are ordered by `at`, and by `id` when the times are equal.\n\nReturn one row per user and session: `user_id`, `session` (1, 2, 3, ... for that user, in time order), `events` (how many events it has), `started_at` and `ended_at` (the first and last `at`). Order by `user_id`, then `session`.",
  "starter": "SELECT user_id, at\nFROM events;\n",
